{"type":"message","id":"7d7bbd50","parentId":"e70e3c4e","timestamp":"2026-10-17T22:49:37.732Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `parse_date`, and all 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` now pass, including `test_dates`.\n\n**Cause:** the format string `\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\"` has nothing that matches the trailing `Z` (the UTC marker), so `strptime` stopped with \"unconverted data remains: Z\".\n\n**Fix:** in `dates/parse.py`, `parse_date` now calls `datetime.fromisoformat(s)`. On Python 3.11 and later, that function accepts `Z`, other offsets like `+02:00`, and timestamps with no offset.\n\nTwo behaviour changes to know about:\n- **Return type:** a timestamp ending in `Z` now comes back with its UTC timezone attached. Timestamps without an offset still come back with no timezone, as before. Comparing or subtracting one of each raises `TypeError`, so any code that mixes them could break. `day_key` is unaffected.\n- **Python version:** this needs Python 3.11 or later; older versions reject `Z`. The project doesn't declare a minimum version, and it ran on 3.13.5 here. If it has to run on older Python, the alternative is to swap a trailing `Z` for `+00:00` before parsing."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":416,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":26855,"totalTokens":27273,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":26855}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792277372551,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011Cg8dG6GEa8hSxPFC8UxCY","duration":5180.068845999998,"ttft":5149.888354999999,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":26857,"nonMessageTokens":21589,"compactionEpoch":0}}}
